3
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:18.950
A line in space can be given as the
intersection of two nonparallel planes.

4
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:25.740
If the planes are not parallel, the general
equation of a line in space

5
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:34.680
can be viewed as a system of general equations
of planes; that is, the line is

6
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:41.360
the locus of points in space whose coordinates
satisfy each equation of the system.

7
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:47.624
It should be said that there are various ways

8
00:00:47.624 --> 00:00:50.890
to give a line in space, and in practice

9
00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:56.730
a line is more often given not by two
intersecting planes but by a direction vector

10
00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:03.370
s parallel to the line and a point M₀ lying on
the line.

11
